      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C237","C204","C201","C215","C212","C200","C236"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct rimantadine-specific absolute oral bioavailability record is supplied.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV AUC comparison is available for the query molecule.",
    "No direct rimantadine hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement is available.",
    "L6 records are analog chemotypes, not rimantadine itself.",
    "Full ionization at pH 7.4 (logD -0.82) leaves permeability uncertainty, though small size and high analog permeability mitigate it."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) with moderate confidence. L5 gut-wall data for small basic amines show high absorptive permeability and no P-gp efflux; L4 Caco-2 data for related small basic amines support high permeability. L6 hepatic-clearance records are analog chemotypes with limited transferability and do not provide affirmative F < 20% evidence."
